      },
      "text": "Chemistry and natural history share a family resemblance: both are about\ncataloging and understanding the diversity of matter and life. The figures here\nrange from the classifiers (Linnaeus giving order to biological chaos) through\nthe discoverers of chemical elements and reactions to the molecular biologists\nwho unified chemistry and biology in the 20th century."
    },
