      "text": "EARLY NATURAL HISTORY              CHEMICAL REVOLUTION\n(1550–1800)                        (1750–1800)\n--------------------               ------------------\nAristotle (first systematic        Priestley (oxygen)\n  natural history)                 Scheele (O₂, Cl₂, acids)\nLinnaeus (taxonomy, binomial       Cavendish (hydrogen)\n  nomenclature)                    Lavoisier (oxygen theory,\nBuffon (biogeography, species        combustion, elements,\n  mutability)                        conservation of mass)\nJohn Ray (species concept,\n  natural theology)"
    },
